      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. A singleton like \"BuildSystemStats\" is the right idea. As per my other comment, it might be OK to only emit information about modules which *are* mixed-build enabled, and leave others off. That is, we need not initialize a map with all enumerated modules and flip flags, but instead simply add mixed-build-enabled module names to a set.\nThe \"Targets\" field you\u0027ve linked is not exactly what you think it is, IIUC. It\u0027s instead the targets that the user has requested be built at \"top-level\". e.g. suppose I want to build the core library `libm`. I\u0027d run `m libc` and that Targets field would contain `libm` only.\n\n2. It *is* an unusual side effect, but I\u0027m not particularly inspired with a better option right now.\n\n3. Yep!",
